{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.saddle_eq_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.saddle_eq_volume","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L132-L138","doc":"Conditional on the (proved-in-the-literature) volume conjecture, the\nKashaev root-of-unity saddle reproduces the figure-eight hyperbolic\nvolume — the keystone Re-face, stated rigorously modulo the named class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjecture41.limit_eq_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjecture41.limit_eq_vol","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L128-L128","doc":"(2π/N)·log ⟨4_1⟩_N → Vol(4_1) as N → ∞. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjecture41.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjecture41.mk","kind":"ctor","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjecture41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjecture41","kind":"class","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L120-L130","doc":"**Volume conjecture for the figure-eight** (Kashaev–Murakami–Murakami),\na PROVED theorem for `4_1` (Andersen–Hansen; Ohtsuki) whose saddle-point /\nBorel-resummation proof is not available in Mathlib. Carried as a §3b-cond\nconditional class: any downstream result may take `[VolumeConjecture41]`\nas an explicit hypothesis. Its single field is the limit identity — the\nRe-face of the keystone `Re V(4_1) = Vol(4_1) → m_μ/m_e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1_decimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1_decimal","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L93-L118","doc":"The 30-digit decimal approximation of `Vol(4_1)`. An APPROXIMATION carrier\n    only — `VOL_4_1 = 2·Cl₂(π/3)` is transcendental; no formal identity between\n    the two is claimed (that would need certified interval arithmetic on `Cl₂`).\n\n    ⚠ **CORRECTED 2026-08-30 (bean `qou-f8lit`) — this literal was WRONG.**\n\nIt read `2.029883212819307250011597804990`, which is **wrong from the 21st significant\nfigure** (error `3.08e-20`) against the canonical\n`2·Cl₂(π/3) = 2.0298832128193072500424051085490…`. Verified by three independent\nroutes: `2·Cl₂(π/3)`, `6·Λ(π/3)`, and `2·Im Li₂(e^{iπ/3})`.\n\n**This is worse in kind than a truncation.** A truncated literal is correct but short;\nthis one presented 30 digits of which only 20 were right, and the extra digits invite\nthe trust that a short value would not get. `MassDerivation.vol_figure_eight` carries the\ncorrect value at 24 digits, so the corpus disagreed with itself.\n\nNothing in Lean was unsound: `abs_VOL_4_1_sub_decimal_lt` bounds the gap by `1/10` and\n`3.08e-20 < 1/10` comfortably, so the theorem held either way — which is exactly why a\ncoarse certified bound does not protect a decimal's digits.\n\nKnown family, partially drained: bean `qou-jgew` found **seven** wrong hand-typed\n`Vol(4₁)` values in one session, and `docs/audits/2026-06-21-q0-clusterD-and-vol41-fixes.md`\nfixed one `.py` probe. Those drains never reached this Lean carrier. **Still live:** six\n`computations/` sites carry the sibling variant `2.0298832128193072500115970029`, one of\nthem a committed witness that needs a producer re-run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1_eq_vol_figure_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1_eq_vol_figure_8","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L89-L91","doc":"`VOL_4_1` agrees with the Clausen-filler volume carrier\n`Vol_figure_8 = 2·Cl₂(π/3)` definitionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VOL_4_1","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L76-L87","doc":"The figure-eight hyperbolic volume constant, EXACT:\n`Vol(4_1) = 2·Cl₂(π/3) = 6·Λ(π/3) ≈ 2.0299` — twice the Clausen value at\nthe Thurston ideal-tetrahedron angle (2 regular ideal tetrahedra of shape\n`e^{iπ/3}`, each of volume `Cl₂(π/3)`).\n\nSTATEMENT-REPAIR NOTE (2026-07-26, bean qou-yf47). This was previously\nthe rational decimal `2.029883212819307250011597804990` — which, as of the\n2026-08-30 correction below, is now known to have been not merely truncated\nbut WRONG from its 21st significant figure. The note is left with the value\nit actually carried; a historical record that silently adopts a later\ncorrection stops being a record. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_pos","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L71-L74","doc":"In particular the Kashaev sum is positive, so `log ⟨4_1⟩_N` is well-defined\nand non-negative for N ≥ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**The Kashaev sum is ≥ 1 for N ≥ 1** — the non-vanishing floor (the k = 0\nterm contributes 1; every other term is ≥ 0). A torus knot would have no\nsuch growth; this is the Lean-checkable base of \"exponential growth ⇒\nnonzero volume rate\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_zero","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The empty (k = 0) product is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The Kashaev product is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.factor_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.factor_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L48-L50","doc":"Each factor `2 - 2·cos x ≥ 0` (since `cos x ≤ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L44-L46","doc":"The figure-eight Kashaev invariant at the N-th root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolume.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The k-fold Kashaev product ∏_{j=1}^k (2 - 2·cos(2πj/N)). ","signatureChunk":0}]}